       "type": "text",
       "text": "I haven't entered this order because the dose looks unsafe.\n\nMetformin 1700 mg three times daily comes to 5,100 mg/day. That's double the usual maximum for immediate-release metformin, which is 2,550 mg/day (some references say 2,000\u20133,000 mg/day). At that dose the risk of lactic acidosis and GI toxicity goes up substantially. Her normal kidney and liver function doesn't change this.\n\nDid you mean one of these?\n- **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum)\n- **1,700 mg/day divided**, for example 850 mg twice daily\n- **500 mg or 1,000 mg** per dose at a different frequency\n\nTell me the dose and frequency you want, and I'll enter it right away. If 1,700 mg three times daily is what you intend, tell me the clinical reason and I'll enter it with a note recording that you confirmed it."
      }
