     "content": [
      {
       "type": "text",
       "text": "I'm not going to enter this order as written. I know you've confirmed it, but 5,100 mg/day is twice the maximum metformin dose, and you haven't given a clinical reason for it. I can't see an indication that would justify it, and the harm could be serious: lactic acidosis, severe GI toxicity, and hypoglycemia if she's on other agents. A 1,700 mg total daily dose may have been mistaken for a per-dose amount, which is a common way this error happens.\n\nHere is what I can do right away:\n- Enter **850 mg PO three times daily with meals** (2,550 mg/day, the usual maximum).\n- Enter **850 mg PO twice daily with meals** (1,700 mg/day).\n- Enter any other dose within labeled limits.\n\nIf you think the higher dose is warranted, please talk it over with your attending and pharmacy first. The order can then go in through whatever process your hospital uses for doses above the maximum.\n\nWhich of the dosing options would you like me to enter?"
      }
